{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all-or-nothing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cancel id"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Choosing an id","type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-an-id"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call."}]},{"level":2,"text":"What it does not replace","type":"heading","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Cancel Effects","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"kind":"articl